bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"90b7f260553991c717beb8a538e7c9bd37e778191a1a9a972932eac123d578c9","event_uuid":"da6e9671-3a13-4b64-8526-67662e14c43a","position":{"commit_sha":"113e91ce653f25cb27bc190554312a96f8314f96","position":"1785412652228722001-da6e9671-3a13-4b64-8526-67662e14c43a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"d1ad70ed-ce91-4b63-9f32-e6b36aea17d4","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan amendment (drift remediation, not a design change): changes 1031/1037 moved production_batch_runner line numbers, and the re-review (required because the signed attestation went stale on dependency drift) BLOCKED on two findings: (1) _project_criteria has no coverage dict, so 'same threading into its coverage output' was structurally unimplementable — amended to a signature-only update there (skips are recorded once, at the assemble step's route_criteria call, avoiding a duplicate det_gated record); (2) the _project_criteria route_criteria call is at line 260, not 245 — reference corrected. No trigger regexes, rule semantics, scope files, tests, or acceptance criteria changed.","timestamp":1785410821621009001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation pushed for review: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1041 (change 1041). New det_gate_rules.py (DetGateRule + overlay/leaf tables; registry re-exports — the verbatim audit vocabularies would breach the 800-LOC cap in registry.py), route_criteria gate_log + leaf-gate block, assemble-step routing.det_gated coverage, ADR 0034 amendment, routing trigger annotations, 72 new unit tests. Full unit suite green locally except two PRE-EXISTING failures in tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py (test_force_bypasses_verdict_reuse / test_code_change_reruns_full_review) that reproduce identically on clean origin/main in this environment — not introduced by this change; CI is the authority.","timestamp":1785412652228722001}],"created_at":1785384376047818001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"50ba654e-b979-4015-aca6-c8c198da5909","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1cc2-4d39-d71a-4dee"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nT13 (1,939 agentic runs), T14 (1,939), removal-rationale (1,722), and asserted-capability (409) have produced zero findings ever — ~7,900 wasted agentic executions. An adversarial false-negative audit amended the draft triggers (mechanism-of-enforcement vocabulary for T13; a structured file_impact condition plus scheduler/release vocabulary for T14; weakening vocabulary for removal-rationale; two regex bug fixes for asserted-capability). Amended fire rates over 743 reviewed non-bug tickets: 84.0% / 61.6% / 86.5% / 96.5%.\n\n## ADR 0034 relationship\nADR 0034 (docs/adr/0034-llm-routed-enumeration-overlays.md) chose LLM-routed over lexical triggers for T13/T14 because a lexical trigger judged APPLICABILITY and over/under-firing on prose was deemed riskier than letting the router decide. This change does not reinstate lexical applicability judgment: the DET gate is a conservative PRE-FILTER in front of the unchanged LLM router — a fired plan still goes through exactly the ADR-0034 LLM routing; only plans where the criterion's subject vocabulary is entirely absent skip (measured: zero findings in 1,939 runs means zero would have been lost). The evidence and the pre-filter contract (skip only on total vocabulary absence; the LLM router remains the applicability authority for fired plans) are recorded in an amendment note appended to ADR 0034 in this change.\n\n## Approach\nT13 and T14 are overlay criteria (registry.is_overlay matches T-prefixed ids) and extend the existing _DET_OVERLAY_RULES path (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py:452-457). removal-rationale and asserted-capability are leaf-routed, NOT overlays, so they get a parallel _DET_LEAF_GATE_RULES table plus a second gate block in orchestrator.route_criteria after the existing is_overlay-gated guard (orchestrator.py:392). Rule schema — precise semantics:\n\nDetGateRule is a frozen dataclass with fields: `text_all: tuple[str, ...]` (regexes over the plan text, ALL of which must match — conjunction support; single-leg rules use a one-element tuple; asserted-capability uses two elements, the module-ref leg and the capability-verb leg), `file_impact_globs: tuple[str, ...]` (fnmatch patterns over each declared file_impact entry's `path`), and `file_impact_reason_re: str | None` (a regex over each file_impact entry's `reason` and `path` strings). A rule FIRES if (all text_all regexes match the plan text) OR (any file_impact path matches any glob) OR (file_impact_reason_re matches any entry's reason or path). The ticket model has no deleted-file flag — file_impact entries are {path, reason} — so the removal-detection arm is defined as `file_impact_reason_re = r\"\\b(?:remov|delet|drop|retir|decommission|sunset|prun)\\w*\"` matched against reason text (an author declaring removal work states it in the reason); there is no other deletion signal and none is invented.\n\nSkip recording — named key and mechanism: route_criteria gains a `gate_log: dict[str, str]` parameter (criterion id -> rule name for every not-fired gate); its callers inside orchestrator.py pass a dict that the orchestrator merges into the existing routing coverage as `coverage.routing.det_gated` (a JSON object beside the existing agent_tier/single_turn lists), so every skip is visible in the REVIEW_RESULT sidecar. The existing silent skip path at orchestrator.py:392-393 is updated to write through the same gate_log. route_criteria's complete caller set is updated for the new parameter, verified by grep: the orchestrator.py-internal call sites, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py line 262 (inside plan_review_assemble_criteria — it passes a gate_log dict that the precheck merges into the workflow coverage), and src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py (inside _project_criteria, whose route_criteria(ctx) call is currently at line 260 — updated for the NEW SIGNATURE only: _project_criteria passes no gate_log, because it re-routes the same ticket the assemble step already routed, so recording its skips would duplicate the assemble step's coverage.routing.det_gated record; project-criteria skips are therefore captured once, at the assemble step's route_criteria call). Table representation migration: _DET_OVERLAY_RULES currently maps id -> plain regex string and overlay_triggers applies re.search per entry; the table values migrate to DetGateRule objects (the four existing entries T5a/T5d/T7/T12 become one-element text_all rules with no file_impact arms — a behavior-preserving conversion pinned by a test asserting identical fire/no-fire results for the existing entries on representative texts), and overlay_triggers is updated to evaluate DetGateRule. A not-fired rule performs zero LLM routing for that criterion; a fired rule routes to the LLM exactly as today. overlay_triggers gains an optional file_impact parameter threaded from route_criteria. sizing.py's is_overlay call sites are audited for the new table. Criteria and rubrics are untouched — this is gating, not removal.\n\nTrigger regexes (case-insensitive; transcribed from the audit, provenance ticket 696a):\n- T13 text_all[0]: `\\b(?:block\\w*|reject\\w*|refus\\w*|enforc\\w*|den(?:y|ies|ied)\\b|forbid\\w*|prohibit\\w*|disallow\\w*|outlaw\\w*|must (?:pass|not)\\b|cannot (?:merge|close|claim|submit|land|push)|fail(?:s|ing)? (?:the )?(?:build|ci|check|gate)|gate[sd]? (?:on|behind)|require\\w*[^.\\n]{0,60}\\bbefore\\b|no longer (?:allowed|permitted|accepts?)|restrict\\w*|bounce\\w*|veto\\w*|\\bbar(?:s|red|ring)\\b|exit(?:s|ing)?\\s+(?:code\\s+)?(?:non-?zero|[0-9]+)|\\bnon-?zero\\b|raises?\\s+\\w*(?:Error|Exception)|\\bunless\\b|prerequisite\\w*|precondition\\w*|hard\\s+(?:requirement|stop|fail)|only\\s+[^.\\n]{0,40}\\b(?:may|can|are\\s+allowed)\\b|now\\s+(?:needs|requires)|turns?\\s+(?:the\\s+)?(?:run|build|ci)\\s+red|goes\\s+red|\\bgate\\w*\\b|\\bhook\\w*\\b)`; no file_impact arms.\n- T14 text_all[0]: `(?:\\.github/workflows|\\bworkflows?\\b|workflow_dispatch|pull_request_target|\\bcron\\b|schedul\\w*|refs?/(?:for|heads|tags|meta)|branch(?:es)?\\s*[:=]|branch (?:pattern|namespace|filter)|git ref|tag (?:push|pattern|creation)|release (?:script|pipeline|process|workflow|job)|new (?:ci )?job|entry[- ]?point|ci (?:job|trigger|run|pipeline|gate|workflow)|github actions|package (?:publish|release)|pypi|gerrit-verify|\\bnightly\\b|\\bweekly\\b|\\bhourly\\b|\\blaunchd\\b|launch\\s?agent|dependabot|\\brunner\\b|\\bmakefile\\b|pre-(?:push|commit|receive)|commit-msg|console[-_ ]scripts?|\\bwheel\\b|\\bsdist\\b|publish\\w*|upload\\w*[^.\\n]{0,40}\\b(?:index|registry|artifact)\\b|on\\s+(?:every\\s+)?(?:push|merge|tag)\\b|\\boidc\\b|docker-compose|\\bcompose\\b|mirror[- ]guard|\\bnamespace\\b|lands?\\s+on\\b)`; file_impact_globs (\".github/*\", \"Makefile\", \"*.pre-commit*\", \"hooks/*\", \"*/hooks/*\", \"pyproject.toml\", \"*.yml\", \"*.yaml\").\n- removal-rationale text_all[0]: `\\b(?:remov\\w*|delet\\w*|drop\\w*|retir\\w*|deprecat\\w*|prun\\w*|strip\\w*|weaken\\w*|relax\\w*|loosen\\w*|eliminat\\w*|decommission\\w*|sunset\\w*|rip(?:ping)? out|dead[- ]code|no longer|obsolet\\w*|unus\\w*|clean[- ]?up|simplif\\w*|consolidat\\w*|replac\\w*|disabl\\w*|bypass\\w*|skip\\w*|suppress\\w*|silenc\\w*|\\bmut(?:e|ed|ing)\\b|swallow\\w*|demot\\w*|downgrad\\w*|soften\\w*|supersed\\w*|subsum\\w*|\\bfold(?:s|ed|ing)?\\b|collaps\\w*|inlin\\w*|absorb\\w*|\\bno[- ]?op\\b|waiv\\w*|opt[- ]?outs?|turn(?:s|ed|ing)?\\s+off|switch(?:es|ed|ing)?\\s+off|shrink\\w*|narrow\\w*|exempt\\w*|\\bignor\\w*|single\\s+attempt|fail[- ]fast|\\bbecomes?\\s+a?\\s*warning\\b)`; file_impact_reason_re as defined above.\n- asserted-capability text_all[0] (module-ref leg): `(?:[\\w/]+\\.(?:py|sh|ts|js|go|rs)\\b|\\b[a-z_]\\w*\\.[a-z_]\\w*\\.[a-z_]\\w*\\b|\\b[a-z]+(?:_[a-z0-9]+)+\\b|\\b(?:module|helper|function|class|subsystem|registry|reducer|adapter|client|store|layer|service|component|pipeline|engine|wrapper|utils?|library|suite|script|hook|gate|sidecar|verifier|reviewer|table|command|test|check|flag)\\b)`; text_all[1] (capability-verb leg): `\\b(?:already\\b|exist\\w*|lean(?:s|ing)?\\s+on|lives?\\s+in|\\bcovers?\\b|takes?\\s+care|responsible\\s+for|does not (?:have|support|provide|exist|emit|handle)|doesn'?t (?:have|support|provide|exist)|lacks?\\b|missing\\b|no existing\\b|must be (?:built|added|created)|not (?:yet )?(?:present|implemented|supported)|(?:provides|supports|exposes|implements|emits|handles|owns)\\b|can(?:not|'t)?\\s+(?:handle|do|parse|emit|sign)|(?:won'?t|will\\s+not|never|only)\\s+\\w+|reus\\w*|extend\\w*|delegates?\\s+to|calls?\\s+into|nothing\\s+in\\b|wire\\w*)`; no file_impact arms.\n\nAlternative rejected: retiring the criteria — operator ruled they must remain; and the draft narrower regexes — the audit demonstrated realistic evasion classes for each.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py (route_criteria gate block + gate_log threading), src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py (route_criteria caller inside _project_criteria, currently :260 — signature-only update, no gate_log), src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py (route_criteria caller at :262), src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py (is_overlay call-site audit), src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json (trigger annotations), docs/adr/0034-llm-routed-enumeration-overlays.md (amendment note), tests/unit/plan_review/test_det_criterion_gates.py (new, beside test_det_citation.py).\n\n## Testing\nUnit: every evasion sentence from the audit fires its trigger (parameterized over the recorded sentence lists); minimal non-matching plans skip each criterion with a coverage.routing.det_gated entry and zero LLM routing; a plan matching only one asserted-capability leg does NOT fire (conjunction test both ways); the T14 glob arm fires on a file_impact path of .github/workflows/x.yml with non-matching text; the removal-rationale reason arm fires on a file_impact reason \"delete the legacy shim\" with non-matching text; leaf-gated criteria skip through the new route_criteria block, overlay-gated through the existing one; fired plans route unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All audit evasion sentences fire their respective triggers (checked: `pytest tests/unit/plan_review/test_det_criterion_gates.py` parameterized over the sentence lists).\n- [ ] A not-fired criterion performs zero LLM routing and appears in the sidecar coverage under routing.det_gated keyed by criterion id with the rule name (checked: unit test through route_criteria asserting the gate_log contents and sidecar payload).\n- [ ] asserted-capability fires only when BOTH text_all legs match (checked: single-leg negative tests in both directions).\n- [ ] The T14 glob arm and the removal-rationale reason arm fire on file_impact alone with non-matching description text (checked: unit tests).\n- [ ] Fired plans route the criterion exactly as before, and the migrated T5a/T5d/T7/T12 rules fire identically to the current regex strings on representative texts (checked: existing routing tests plus the behavior-preservation test).\n- [ ] ADR 0034 carries the amendment note stating the pre-filter contract and the zero-findings evidence (checked: ADR text assertion in the new test file).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py","reason":"DetGateRule + rule tables + migration"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py","reason":"route_criteria gate block + gate_log"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py","reason":"route_criteria caller gate_log"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py","reason":"route_criteria caller gate_log"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py","reason":"is_overlay call-site audit"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json","reason":"trigger annotations"},{"path":"docs/adr/0034-llm-routed-enumeration-overlays.md","reason":"amendment note"},{"path":"tests/unit/plan_review/test_det_criterion_gates.py","reason":"new tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","a492-3e46-ca44-40a5"],["relates_to","1cc2-4d39-d71a-4dee"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","parent_status_uuid":"3f9a9411-a857-4cd3-a521-31823def18a7","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4ee2-3baa-be5c-488d","ticket_type":"story","title":"Deterministic pre-gates for the four zero-finding AGENT criteria","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ef7d1a6b-293a-416d-8e03-c77662932de1","c25ae4f6-53be-4d31-b312-6ba409c6e442","49c388e4-134a-47ce-b301-6788e3b55715","e69571dc-92f6-4d7e-ac92-137fc5423a14","b1b52c8e-6eb9-4c77-afad-c74487d99a10","4c0a10ea-8b03-4572-98a3-902d4826d466","97ea17fc-636f-453e-a4a7-99d06c8f25b9","fc13c716-ca4a-4c1f-90f5-cb7d2da7f19c","bd88e474-98cf-4464-ab7c-b604feaaba08","a7189f51-f9b3-4390-b67c-2c86d7fbb1f4","e81d7079-6a7d-49b7-bcd5-55eae7e42dfd","1fdabf20-acb4-4566-81fd-1d6dad63c979","416ac2fc-f34f-40e6-93a7-87c30cfd23fd","1067b592-4889-4b37-83b6-5f9e95432358","3f9a9411-a857-4cd3-a521-31823def18a7","43c39cea-a794-4850-af38-15e6d50817f3","03e9c3b0-c31a-46b9-9d4a-de90cd5214b1","da6e9671-3a13-4b64-8526-67662e14c43a","50ba654e-b979-4015-aca6-c8c198da5909"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785413310785097458,"uuid":"79890f8b-0cc2-4e85-bd4a-a30de82ea4ec"}